# NOTE: the compose files build the lab image with the context one level UP
# (task1/, see docker-compose.override.yml), and Docker reads only the
# .dockerignore at the context root, so task1/.dockerignore is the governing
# file. This one applies only to a direct `docker build task1/lab`, which the
# Dockerfile's COPY of ../assessment makes fail anyway. Kept in step with the
# governing file so no future context change ships notes, tests or caches.
notes
**/tests
**/.git
**/data
**/models
**/results
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.Trash*
**/*.zip
**/*.tgz
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.tar
**/devonly*
